# Proxy-eval sweep parameters (read by .github/workflows/proxy-eval.yml, job `params`).
#
# 2026-09-17 (session 13) - THE FIELD THAT SHIPS.
#
# Why this run: the emission decision now says SHIP the measured policy (floor 0.1, thin, width 0
# px), from condition 3 being met on the ensemble-2 sweep.  But the submission is not any single
# ensemble's field: it is the mean of the live fold sets, and the floor is a threshold on that
# mean.  The two sweeps so far measured each ensemble SEPARATELY, so neither is the field the
# policy will be applied to.  This run re-blends ensembles 1 and 2 into ONE mean (the multi-run
# support added in 052f821: RUN_ID=a,b,c downloads folds/folds2/folds3 and blends all of them with
# --save-ensemble) and sweeps that field with the identical grid.
#
# What it can change: if floor 0.1 stops beating the shipped policy by > 0.01 on this field, or the
# per-floor optimum moves, the decision record will say so and the adoption is re-opened.  What it
# cannot do is flatter the candidate: the sweep's acceptance control (a catalogue-copy submission
# must score 0 on the proxy-only truth) is checked before any candidate is scored.
#
# Ensemble 3 (run 35263581931) is deliberately NOT in this list yet: its fold 0 is still training
# and a fold set that changes under the measurement is not a measurement.  It can join a later
# blend together with its own sweep.
